 "notes": "Recomputed with fresh standard-library python (no import of lab/analyze.py) from results/episodes/*.jsonl and results/dev_final/*.jsonl. 2074 comparisons against results/summary.json and the integrity expectations. Zero mismatches at the stated tolerances (exact on counts, 0.002 on rates and Wilson interval ends, 0.01 on bootstrap interval ends). All pass counts, Wilson intervals, paired differences, regressed/improved counts and exact McNemar p values match for 9 conditions vs baseline overall and in 90 condition-by-family cells, for the 2 matched-control comparisons overall and by family, for the difficulty table, for the dev set (10 conditions x 100 tasks) and for totals. 3 by-family Holm-adjusted p values differ from mine by 0.000030 to 0.000039 (listed under rounding_differences_below_tolerance): summary.json applies Holm to p values already rounded to 6 decimals, I applied it to unrounded p values. All 3 are below 0.004 either way and inside the 0.002 tolerance, so they are not counted as mismatches. Display caveat: summary.json shows mcnemar_p 0.0 and mcnemar_p_holm 0 for ffn_med, ffn_up_low, rand_ffn_med and rand_attn_med vs baseline; these are values rounded to 6 decimals, the unrounded values are under vs_baseline_exact_mcnemar_p_unrounded and should be reported as p < 0.000001. Integrity: each of the 10 held-out files has 1000 records, 1000 unique task ids, the same id set as baseline and as tasks/suite_eval.jsonl, 100 tasks in each of 10 families, 0 status=error, 0 status other than ok, 0 scores outside 0/1, and 0 records whose artifact_sha256 differs from manifests/conditions/<condition>.json. noop and rollback manifests carry the same artifact sha256 as baseline, and their replies, final, trace, prompt_shown and score equal baseline on 1000 of 1000 tasks. Dev files: 100 records, 100 unique ids, same id set, 0 non-ok status, 0 sha mismatches per condition; 0 task ids shared between dev and held-out. Not checked here: whether the score field itself is correct (scores were taken as recorded, the checker was not rerun), the per-condition metrics blocks, latency and output_changed fields. Bootstrap intervals use my own resampling and seed, so they agree with summary.json only within the 0.01 tolerance.",
